# Install with visudo as /etc/sudoers.d/rad-deploy. Grants the SSH-only
# `rad-deploy` account the exact same narrow privilege already reviewed for
# `rad-runner` in rad-runner.sudoers - invoking the release broker with no
# arguments (the broker reads its request from stdin only). The empty
# argument string is essential (not a wildcard): it is what forces every
# invocation through scripts/production/rad_release.py's stdin-JSON path and
# blocks the separate (and intentionally sudoers-forbidden) `rollback
# <transaction>` argv mode - that mode is reserved for a root operator typing
# it directly, never for an account reachable over SSH.
#
# rad-deploy itself has no other privileges: no shell login beyond this one
# forced SSH command (see rad-deploy-ssh-entrypoint.sh and the
# authorized_keys line in docs/vps-tailscale-ssh-deploy.md), no group
# memberships beyond its own, and no access to /opt/rad*, /etc/rad*, or
# Docker except through this exact sudo rule.
Defaults:rad-deploy env_reset, !setenv
rad-deploy ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/rad-release ""
